## 5. API contract expected by the screens

Check that your existing backend returns these response shapes. If your Module 36 routes use different response wrappers, adjust the frontend parsing rather than silently treating missing data as an empty list.

| Endpoint                                  | Method | Expected behaviour                                            |
| ----------------------------------------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `/api/chatbot-admin/knowledge`            | GET    | Return `{ articles: [] }`                                     |
| `/api/chatbot-admin/knowledge`            | POST   | Create a draft article                                        |
| `/api/chatbot-admin/knowledge/:id`        | PATCH  | Update article fields                                         |
| `/api/chatbot-admin/knowledge/:id/status` | PATCH  | Publish, unpublish or archive                                 |
| `/api/chatbot-admin/escalations`          | GET    | Return `{ escalations: [] }`, including conversation messages |
| `/api/chatbot-admin/escalations/:id`      | PATCH  | Update status and/or resolution                               |

Backend requirements to verify:

- All requests must be authenticated and authorized server-side.
- Every database query must be scoped to the administrator's institution.
- Only authorized roles should publish knowledge articles.
- Only authorized customer-care staff should view visitor contact information and transcripts.
- The `ASSIGNED` action must set `assignedToId` to the authenticated administrator, not an ID supplied by the browser.
- Validate status transitions and resolution lengths on the server.
- Record status changes and assignment actions in the audit log.
- Prefer archiving knowledge articles over permanent deletion.

